 & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot (5-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{5}^{a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y={5}^{x}$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{5}^{x}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{5}^{x}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042659/assets/06c51ecc423683f4377248004b7a318f1348836bd752a7f65f94457d1774e64d.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}2\\cdot {5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot (5-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{5}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot (5-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317047 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e84d5ab0-cec4-5988-9db3-8e296590d279" :knowledge-point/title "Improper Integral Involving Other Exponential Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a68b6822-d4c4-57bb-ab62-e78daf46aa92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317049} {:answer/id #uuid "d5a478f2-f2c0-53c4-a58e-3ec9acc13f4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317050} {:answer/id #uuid "e90941e6-aad3-5bea-acf4-ebcf03514f21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317051} {:answer/id #uuid "d5a6efce-c5a0-514c-8cb1-3b5c46335b51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The integral diverges" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317052} {:answer/id #uuid "5f462d65-35a6-53bb-a559-10bfba3050d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f462d65